From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:54:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: guard truncated TXFREE events

MT7996 firmware can occasionally emit a TXFREE event whose MSDU count is
larger than the payload actually present.  Returning immediately skips the
normal tail cleanup and leaks completed skbs and tokens.  Break out of the
descriptor loop after the valid prefix and fall through to the normal
cleanup path; the malformed remainder is dropped without a WARN splat.

Signed-off-by: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1382,9 +1382,9 @@ mt7996_mac_tx_free(struct mt7996_dev *dev, void *data, int len)
 	for (cur_info = &tx_free[2]; count < total; cur_info++) {
 		u32 msdu, info;
 		u8 i;
 
-		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end))
-			return;
+		if ((void *)cur_info >= end)
+			break;
 		/* 1'b1: new wcid pair.
 		 * 1'b0: msdu_id with the same 'wcid pair' as above.
 		 */
